Why AGPL-3.0
------------
Two separate obligations force a copyleft, AGPLv3-compatible license on the whole program:

1. NoteDigger (https://github.com/madderscientist/noteDigger) is licensed GPL-3.0 and is used as
   the reference implementation, including verbatim reuse of code. GPLv3 section 13 permits
   combining a GPLv3 work with an AGPLv3 work into a single combined work; the result is
   conveyed under the AGPLv3 terms.
2. namioto/tempo.py reimplements the TempoCNN front end described by Essentia
   (https://essentia.upf.edu, AGPL-3.0). Keeping the program under AGPLv3 stays compliant
   whether or not that module is judged to be a derivative of Essentia's implementation.

The GUI uses PySide6, available under LGPL-3.0/GPL-3.0 or a commercial license. The program's
AGPL-3.0 license is required by the NoteDigger and Essentia-derived code described above.


